# Godoc

Follow [.cursor/skills/godoc/SKILL.md](../skills/godoc/SKILL.md).

- Every exported `func`, `type`, `const`, `var`, and method needs a godoc comment.
- Comments are complete sentences starting with the name of the thing described.
- Package-level overview goes in `doc.go` when it helps readers.
- CI fails on undocumented exports via golangci-lint revive `exported` (public
  API only). Unexported helpers do not need godoc for CI.
- Ignore CodeRabbit private/unexported docstring coverage %; it is not a gate
  and must not drive PR changes.

Browse locally: `go doc github.com/sviatsviatsviat/wat/<package>`
